# The shared analysis of the collections (D409, #866) on the
# programs of `main`, at the place of the collection-level transformations:
# the IR of the rhombic dodecahedron with groups and with the matrix,
# stopped after md-alg-transform-collections, printed by the test pass.
# No sort of these programs is redundant; for each, what blocks it, which
# is where #869 starts:
#
# - mdrt_gpu_matrix_sort, the stable rank into a buffer of its own: a
#   kernel reads that buffer by index (rule 1). The scatter before it
#   writes its order into an argument of the function (rule 3).
# - mdrt_gpu_spatial_order, the counting sort by the numbers of the input:
#   its order is an argument of the function, read by the caller (rule 3).
# - The groups build's two counting sorts (particles by column and z-bin;
#   places by cell of the search grid): their orders are local, read by
#   md_alg.bin_item alone, which hands its user the item at a place and so
#   requires the layout. Their users form groups of consecutive particles
#   in z, so the order is observed: no declared reader (md_alg.bin_members)
#   would state less.
#
# The slot pass runs the same analysis and changes nothing.
#
# REQUIRES: cuda
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/triclinic/water.top %S/Inputs/triclinic/dodecahedron.gro %t/
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %S/md-alg-passes-gpu.test | sed '1d;$d' > %t/groups.toml
# RUN: sed 's/^neighbor_structure = "GROUPS"/neighbor_structure = "MATRIX"/' %t/groups.toml > %t/matrix.toml
# RUN: cd %t && mdir emit groups.toml --stage=pipeline | sed 's/,convert-md-alg-to-gpu,.*//' > groups.slot
# RUN: cd %t && mdir emit matrix.toml --stage=pipeline | sed 's/,convert-md-alg-to-gpu,.*//' > matrix.slot
# RUN: cd %t && sh -c 'MDIR_PIPELINE="$(cat groups.slot)" mdir emit groups.toml --stage=lowered' > groups.slot.mlir
# RUN: cd %t && sh -c 'MDIR_PIPELINE="$(cat matrix.slot)" mdir emit matrix.toml --stage=lowered' > matrix.slot.mlir
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/groups.slot.mlir --test-md-alg-print-collections -o /dev/null > %t/groups.facts
# RUN: mdir-opt %t/matrix.slot.mlir --test-md-alg-print-collections -o /dev/null > %t/matrix.facts
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=COMMON,GROUPS < %t/groups.facts
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COMMON < %t/matrix.facts
# No sort is redundant, in either program; four sorts in the one, two in
# the other.
# RUN: not grep ': redundant:' %t/groups.facts %t/matrix.facts
# RUN: grep -c '^  sort ' %t/groups.facts | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FOUR
# RUN: grep -c '^  sort ' %t/matrix.facts | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TWO
# FOUR: 4
# TWO: 2

# The matrix sort: the scatter's order is an argument; the stable rank's,
# local, is read by index in the kernel that follows.
# COMMON-LABEL: md_alg collections of @mdrt_gpu_matrix_sort
# COMMON:      collection out of md_alg.scatter_to_bins at {{[0-9]+}}: %[[SCATTERED:[^ ]+]]
# COMMON-NEXT:   root: %[[SCATTERED]], not allocated here, aliases 0
# COMMON-NEXT:   escapes: an argument of the function
# COMMON-NEXT:   guarantees: grouped_by(%[[CELLS:[^)]+]])
# COMMON-NEXT:   use: md_alg.sort_bins at {{[0-9]+}}: read, requires grouped_by(%[[CELLS]]), streamed (orders each bin itself)
# COMMON-NEXT:   use: memref.store at {{[0-9]+}}: write, requires layout (a write by index)
# COMMON-NEXT:   requires: layout
# COMMON:        determinism: unordered
# COMMON:      collection out of md_alg.sort_bins at {{[0-9]+}}: %[[RANKED:[^ ]+]]
# COMMON-NEXT:   root: %[[RANKED]], allocated at {{[0-9]+}}, aliases 1
# COMMON-NEXT:   escapes: no
# COMMON-NEXT:   guarantees: stable(%[[CELLS]], item)
# COMMON-NEXT:   use: memref.load at {{[0-9]+}}: read, requires layout, random (a read by index)
# COMMON-NEXT:   use: gpu.dealloc at {{[0-9]+}}: release
# COMMON-NEXT:   requires: layout
# COMMON-NEXT:   access: random
# COMMON-NEXT:   cardinality: run-time
# COMMON-NEXT:   lifetime: produced at {{[0-9]+}}, last use at {{[0-9]+}}, released at {{[0-9]+}}
# COMMON-NEXT:   determinism: bitwise
# COMMON-NEXT: sort md_alg.sort_bins at {{[0-9]+}}: not redundant: requires layout, without the sort grouped_by(%[[CELLS]]), with it stable(%[[CELLS]], item); the order is not met without it; a consumer does not combine exactly

# The spatial order: into an argument.
# COMMON-LABEL: md_alg collections of @mdrt_gpu_spatial_order
# COMMON:      collection out of md_alg.sort_by_key at {{[0-9]+}}: %[[SPATIAL:[^ ]+]]
# COMMON-NEXT:   root: %[[SPATIAL]], not allocated here, aliases 0
# COMMON-NEXT:   escapes: an argument of the function
# COMMON-NEXT:   guarantees: stable(%[[SS:[^,]+]], %[[NUMBERS:[^)]+]])
# COMMON-NEXT:   requires: layout
# COMMON:      sort md_alg.sort_by_key at {{[0-9]+}}: not redundant: requires layout, without the sort grouped_by(%[[SS]]), with it stable(%[[SS]], %[[NUMBERS]]); the order is not met without it; a consumer does not combine exactly

# The groups build: each order local, read by md_alg.bin_item alone, and
# released.
# GROUPS-LABEL: md_alg collections of @mdrt_gpu_build_neighbors_groups_triclinic
# GROUPS:      collection out of md_alg.sort_by_key at {{[0-9]+}}: %[[COLUMNS:[^ ]+]]
# GROUPS-NEXT:   root: %[[COLUMNS]], allocated at {{[0-9]+}}, aliases 1
# GROUPS-NEXT:   escapes: no
# GROUPS-NEXT:   guarantees: stable(%[[CS:[^,]+]], item)
# GROUPS-NEXT:   use: md_alg.bin_item at {{[0-9]+}}: read, requires layout, gathered (reads the item at a place)
# GROUPS-NEXT:   use: md_alg.bin_item at {{[0-9]+}}: read, requires layout, gathered (reads the item at a place)
# GROUPS-NEXT:   use: gpu.dealloc at {{[0-9]+}}: release
# GROUPS-NEXT:   requires: layout
# GROUPS-NEXT:   access: gathered
# GROUPS-NEXT:   cardinality: bound %{{.*}}
# GROUPS-NEXT:   lifetime: produced at {{[0-9]+}}, last use at {{[0-9]+}}, released at {{[0-9]+}}
# GROUPS-NEXT:   determinism: bitwise
# GROUPS-NEXT: sort md_alg.sort_by_key at {{[0-9]+}}: not redundant: requires layout, without the sort grouped_by(%[[CS]]), with it stable(%[[CS]], item); the order is not met without it{{$}}
# GROUPS:      collection out of md_alg.sort_by_key at {{[0-9]+}}: %[[CELLORDER:[^ ]+]]
# GROUPS-NEXT:   root: %[[CELLORDER]], allocated at {{[0-9]+}}, aliases 1
# GROUPS-NEXT:   escapes: no
# GROUPS-NEXT:   guarantees: stable(%[[GS:[^,]+]], item)
# GROUPS-NEXT:   use: md_alg.bin_item at {{[0-9]+}}: read, requires layout, gathered (reads the item at a place)
# GROUPS-NEXT:   use: md_alg.bin_item at {{[0-9]+}}: read, requires layout, gathered (reads the item at a place)
# GROUPS-NEXT:   use: gpu.dealloc at {{[0-9]+}}: release
# GROUPS-NEXT:   requires: layout
# GROUPS:      sort md_alg.sort_by_key at {{[0-9]+}}: not redundant: requires layout, without the sort grouped_by(%[[GS]]), with it stable(%[[GS]], item); the order is not met without it{{$}}
